Usage: semaphore-cli publish verify [flags]

Check the manifest and every object it lists in the bucket

Reads the manifest and every listed object of the connection, and checks size,
checksum, the content of each document, and that every flag-set source resolves.
It never writes. Exit code 5 when a problem is found.

Flags:
  -h, --help                   Show context-sensitive help.
  -v, --version                Print the version and exit

  -c, --config=STRING          bootstrap file whose controlPlane connection is
                               the target
      --bucket=STRING          bucket (without --config)
      --prefix=STRING          key prefix of the objects and of the default
                               manifest key
      --region=STRING          AWS region (without --config)
      --endpoint=STRING        S3 endpoint, for emulators and S3 compatible
                               stores (without --config)
      --channel=STRING         channel of the manifest (without --config;
                               default stable)
      --connection=STRING      connection name written in the manifest (without
                               --config; default control)
      --manifest-key=STRING    manifest key (without --config; default
                               <prefix>manifests/<channel>.yaml)
  -o, --output="text"          output format: text or json
      --generation=0           generation to write (default: the one in the
                               bucket plus one)
      --dry-run                plan the publication: the same reads, no write
      --replace-invalid-manifest
                               replace a manifest in the bucket that is invalid
                               or over the limits (needs --generation)
